{
  "requirement": "`habeas_sdk::graph` defines the graph's associated types:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Graph: Send + Sync {\n    /// The *identifier* identifies a particular node in the graph.\n    type NodeId: Clone + Eq + Send + Sync;\n\n    /// The *label* on an edge defines the kind of relationship\n    /// between two nodes.\n    type EdgeLabel: Clone + Send + Sync;\n\n    /// Application-defined errors from graph operations.\n    type Error: Send;\n\n    // ... additional methods defined below ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement `requirements.sdk.graph.domain_types` states these obligations:\n\n- `Graph: Send + Sync`.\n- `NodeId: Clone + Eq + Send + Sync`.\n- `EdgeLabel: Clone + Send + Sync`.\n- `Error: Send`.\n\n`crates/habeas-sdk/tests/contracts.rs#fn[graph_relationships_work_without_node_contents_or_storage]` covers all of them with two techniques.\n\n- **Required bounds (a bound must not be loosened).** The inner `check_bounds::<G: Graph>` helper is generic and uses only the `Graph` bound. It asserts `send_sync::<G>`, `identity::<G::NodeId>` (Clone + Eq + Send + Sync), `label::<G::EdgeLabel>` (Clone + Send + Sync) and `error::<G::Error>` (Send). If the trait dropped any of these bounds, the test would not compile. It is instantiated with `check_bounds::<Relationships>()`.\n- **No extra bounds (a bound must not be added).** The fixture types are deliberately minimal.\n  - `Identity` is only Clone + PartialEq + Eq.\n  - `Label` is only Clone.\n  - `GraphError` wraps a `Cell`, so it is Send but not Sync, and it is not Debug, Clone or `std::error::Error`.\n  - Adding `Sync` to `Error`, or `Debug`, `Hash` or similar to the other types, would therefore stop the fixture from implementing `Graph`.\n\nThe test also exercises the associated types in use: `outgoing_edges` returns `Vec<NodeId>`, a labelled lookup works, and an `Error` value is returned and moved through `send(...)`.\n\nOther tests give extra support. The tests in `src/sdk.rs` (`habeas_paths_preserve_opaque_segments_and_separate_all_node_kinds`, `requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk`) and `src/authoring/sdk.rs` (`review_graph_delegates_unprepared_sources_and_paths_to_the_domain`) use the real Habeas domain as a `Graph` implementation. The `agent.rs` and `contracts.rs` tests do the same for the `Memory` and `Application` domains. None of these is needed for the bounds checks.\n\nI found no obligation in the requirement text that lacks a test. The text does not mention `'static` or other bounds, so I did not treat their absence as a gap.",
